# oracle-change: code-change's template, except that someone answers. On the Harbor
# arm the run is the simulated user's, so the template ends in its one run.
provider {{provider}}
harness {{harness}}
approval default deny
approval bash dotnet *
approval bash cd * && dotnet *
approval bash git *
approval bash ls *
approval bash cat *
approval bash find *
approval bash grep *
approval bash rg *
approval bash head *
approval bash tail *
approval bash wc *
# The same reads behind a cd: Haiku's first call is usually `cd /app && find …`, and a
# denial there cost whole runs their bash (breitreiter/nb#2).
approval bash cd * && git *
approval bash cd * && ls *
approval bash cd * && cat *
approval bash cd * && find *
approval bash cd * && grep *
approval bash cd * && rg *
approval bash cd * && head *
approval bash cd * && tail *
approval bash cd * && wc *
loop 3
budget tool_calls 60
budget wall_ms 1800000
system You are a software engineer working in the repository at {{work}}, which is your \
current directory. It is a small .NET project with tests. Make the change described \
below, keep the existing tests passing, and add or update tests where the change \
warrants it. Use the file tools to read and edit; use bash for `dotnet build` and \
`dotnet test`. The person who asked for the change is available: if the request leaves \
out something you need to decide, stop and ask them, then carry on with their answer. \
Finish with a short summary of what you changed and the test result.
run {{prompt}}
